@StefanoRaggi after some extensive testing: yes you are correct the issue still happens prior to [#4317](https://github.com/QuantConnect/Lean/pull/4317). For example, the same problem happens with this commit [0b3ecea4d74a0c785e98b111d5ea2a3999820866](https://github.com/QuantConnect/Lean/commit/0b3ecea4d74a0c785e98b111d5ea2a3999820866)

More experimentation shows that the 2020-03-31 version of LEAN seems to work fine and reconnects properly (at least after a few hours testing): [f47e3612274973fd7c72ee0b1720956db3987cd7](https://github.com/QuantConnect/Lean/tree/f47e3612274973fd7c72ee0b1720956db3987cd7)
The even earlier version we were using in prod failed a few days ago as Coinbase stopped supporting older TLS, but that one (March 31) seems to [already have](https://github.com/QuantConnect/Lean/commit/2f2b2624d499ffcc6a65afd2f03c391b4728a8a5) proper TLS12 support.
